# Build-context whitelist for `podman build` (== .dockerignore).
#
# Every image Containerfile (containers/Containerfile.*) COPYs only bin/,
# config/, and tests/.  The build context, however, is the whole repo root, and
# that root also holds tens of GB of local artifacts -- test-pixi/ (~26G),
# deploy/ (~12G, gitignored), python/ (a spaxi checkout), meta/, etc.  Without
# this file podman tars ALL of it before running the first step, spinning for
# tens of minutes reading the context (no build output, no compilers, just a
# pegged podman) -- which looks exactly like a hang.
#
# So exclude everything, then re-include only the three trees the images copy.
# Keep this in sync with the COPY lines if a Containerfile ever needs more.
*
!bin
!config
!tests
